From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3528: Add the DMC

The memory controller scales the DDR through the trusted firmware,
counting its load with the DFI. Its rates and their voltages depend on
the DDR a board carries, so the board fills the OPP table and names the
controller's supply.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
index 2aad7bb..59b54c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528.dtsi
@@ -166,6 +166,20 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	dmc: memory-controller {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rk3528-dmc";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 17 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		interrupt-names = "complete";
+		clocks = <&scmi_clk SCMI_CLK_DDR>;
+		devfreq-events = <&dfi>;
+		operating-points-v2 = <&dmc_opp_table>;
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
+	dmc_opp_table: opp-table-dmc {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+	};
+
 	pinctrl: pinctrl {
 		compatible = "rockchip,rk3528-pinctrl";
 		rockchip,grf = <&ioc_grf>;
